function reverseMove(b: Board, player: Player, am: AppliedMove) {
  const sign = player === "white" ? 1 : -1;
  const opp = opponent(player);
  const oppSign = -sign;
  if (am.from === BAR) b.bar[player]++;
  else b.points[am.from] += sign;
  if (am.to === OFF) { b.off[player]--; return; }
  b.points[am.to] -= sign;
  if (am.hit) {
    b.bar[opp]--;
    b.points[am.to] += oppSign;
  }
}
```
Check correctness: For to in range, we removed player sign. If hit, point had one player and opponent was removed. After subtract sign, point becomes 0. Add oppSign makes -sign or +sign. Good. If not hit, subtract sign just reduces count; should remain correct because before move point had at least one own checker. Good.

